WHATNOW

What tam-last is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W16


STATE

  Version 0.2.3 on branch dev (Phase P3 complete; Fred accepted 0.2.3 on
  2026-11-23, W16). Implemented and verified:
  - Shared Wayland display & multi-window layer (include/tam-last/window.h,
    src/window.c, include/tam-last/proto.h, src/wl/proto.c): split
    tl_display (one Wayland connection, globals, seat focus routing for
    keyboard/pointer/IME, clipboard/primary selection, repeat info) from
    per-window tl_window (surfaces, toplevels, viewports, fractional scale,
    SHM buffers, clean per-window Wayland object destruction).
  - Shared font cache (include/tam-last/font.h, src/font/font.c):
    reference-counted tl_font_cache keyed by font paths, point size, and
    dpi with warm LRU retention (up to 8 unreferenced entries) so new
    windows reuse mapped TTF files, sibling/fallback faces, and glyph
    masks immediately.
  - Multi-window PTY isolation (include/tam-last/pty.h, src/pty.c):
    tl_pty_spawn_in applies client cwd, SHELL, and $TERM in the child
    without mutating the server process.
  - Client/server Unix-socket IPC (include/tam-last/ipc.h, src/ipc.c):
    length-prefixed, bounds-checked protocol over
    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tam-last-<WAYLAND_DISPLAY>.sock (or -S/--socket),
    owner-only (0600) permissions, live-server vs stale-socket detection,
    --server, --client (and installed tam-last-client symlink), and
    -N/--no-wait. Fails with a clear error if no server is running.
  - Unified multi-window poll() event loop in src/main.c (timeout-free
    when idle, bounded client handshake deadlines, clean SIGINT/SIGTERM
    shutdown and socket unlinking).
  - Interactive sandbox/demo-server (option d in sandbox/play).

  make test (test_wire 192, test_vt 431, test_ttf 3036, test_keys 266,
